# GitNexus ignore rules - standard template for large Drupal 11 repos
# Drupal core + contrib + vendor account for the large majority of PHP files
# in these repos (10,000-11,000+ files in core alone) and are what push
# GitNexus's call-graph resolution into OOM/hang territory on a full index.
# Custom code (the part actually worth indexing) is a small fraction of the
# total file count. Exclude core/contrib/vendor and index custom code only.
#
# Typical breakdown for a mid-size Drupal 11 site: core ~10,000-11,000 files,
# contrib ~3,000-4,000, vendor ~8,000-14,000, custom code often under 150.
# Adjust paths below if a repo's directory layout differs (check html/web/
# vs a different docroot name before assuming this applies as-is).

# === DRUPAL CORE & CONTRIB (managed by Composer, not hand-edited) ===
html/web/core/
html/web/modules/contrib/
html/web/themes/contrib/
html/web/profiles/contrib/

# === VENDOR DEPENDENCIES ===
html/vendor/
html/web/vendor/
vendor/

# === NODE.JS DEPENDENCIES ===
node_modules/
puppeteer/node_modules/

# === BUILD ARTIFACTS & GENERATED ===
html/web/sites/default/files/
html/web/sites/default/settings.local.php
.build/
dist/
build/

# === LARGE BINARY/COMPILED FILES ===
*.phar
*.jar
*.zip
*.gz

# === LOCK FILES (bloat without value to call-graph analysis) ===
composer.lock
package-lock.json

# === IDE & SYSTEM ===
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
*.log
